WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.251 --> 00:00:04.671
 Got a lot of snow 
 to get rid of. 

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:07.382
 Time to get 
 a new outhouse built. 

00:00:07.382 --> 00:00:10.135
 It's something I need right now. 

00:00:10.135 --> 00:00:13.221
 This summer I went ahead and dug 
 a couple different holes 

00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:14.931
 around the property, 

00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:18.685
 but my wrist was broke 
 in an accident this fall. 

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.270
 I'm starting to recover finally 

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.772
 to where I can, you know, 
 start doing projects like this, 

00:00:22.772 --> 00:00:25.942
 and now I gotta go dig out 
 all the blown-in, drifted snow 

00:00:25.942 --> 00:00:27.944
 before I can get started. 

00:00:27.944 --> 00:00:32.032
 ♪  

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:34.159
 There we go, 
 I'm into the hole now, 

00:00:34.159 --> 00:00:37.746
 there's the framing that I used 
 to shore up the sides, 

00:00:37.746 --> 00:00:39.330
 that way 
 when the ground's thawed 

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:42.459
 it can't just slough in 
 and be filling up the hole. 

00:00:43.918 --> 00:00:46.504
 This might not seem like 
 a very fancy bathroom, 

00:00:46.504 --> 00:00:49.883
 but I look around and I think, 

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.926
 man, this is 
 the perfect setting. 

00:00:51.926 --> 00:00:54.971
 Feel like you're out here 
 in the middle of nowhere. 

00:00:54.971 --> 00:00:58.433
 It's nice, not too far a walk 
 from my place, but far enough, 

00:00:58.433 --> 00:00:59.642
 you know, you don't want 
 to have your outhouse 

00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:01.853
 too close to your house. 

00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:03.563
 You don't want the smell, 
 you know, 

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:08.234
 although I'm gonna use some 
 sawdust to keep the smell down. 

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:11.988
 Let's talk about it like it is, 
 you know. Gotta poop. 

00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:14.741
 [laughs] 

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:18.995
 ♪  

00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:22.624
 Alright, got this 
 nice and dug out here 

00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:25.335
 and good little 
 workspace and area. 

00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:29.672
 Next step, go get some 
 materials, start my build. 

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:33.093
 Hang on, bud. 

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:38.515
 ♪  

00:01:38.515 --> 00:01:40.558
 I'm gonna head down 
 into the woods here, 

00:01:40.558 --> 00:01:43.394
 find a spot to get myself 
 all the posts and crosspieces 

00:01:43.394 --> 00:01:46.356
 that I'm gonna need for 
 the structure of the outhouse. 

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:48.358
 ♪  

00:01:48.358 --> 00:01:54.948
 ♪  

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:58.034
 Oh, yeah, that's it right there. 

00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:03.498
 Alright, this tree right here 
 is nice and dead. 

00:02:03.498 --> 00:02:07.085
 It's got, uh, looks like all 
 the pieces that I'm gonna need. 

00:02:10.338 --> 00:02:14.217
 You stay, Neil, you stay 
 right there. Good boy. 

00:02:14.217 --> 00:02:17.887
 ♪  

00:02:17.887 --> 00:02:20.515
 This is what you call 
 my lumberyard right here. 

00:02:21.891 --> 00:02:23.309
 Some people see 
 the disadvantages 

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:26.187
 of living out in the bush. 

00:02:26.187 --> 00:02:28.439
 I look at the advantages of it. 

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:33.820
 If I need to go get 
 some wood to work with, 

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.072
 it's right here in my backyard. 

00:02:36.072 --> 00:02:38.116
 ♪  

00:02:38.116 --> 00:02:44.956
 ♪  

00:02:44.956 --> 00:02:46.791
 Alright! 

00:02:46.791 --> 00:02:49.752
 ♪  

00:02:49.752 --> 00:02:52.964
 The goal is just to make 
 a simple outhouse. 

00:02:52.964 --> 00:02:56.301
 I'm just gonna use what I got 
 around me, spruce poles, 

00:02:56.301 --> 00:02:59.554
 and I kinda like that look 
 aesthetically as well. 

00:03:01.431 --> 00:03:04.058
 I've got all my pieces here 
 for my outhouse, 

00:03:04.058 --> 00:03:05.101
 they were all in one tree, 

00:03:05.101 --> 00:03:06.811
 that gave me a bunch 
 of firewood, too, 

00:03:06.811 --> 00:03:10.607
 so, just couldn't get it 
 better than that. 

00:03:10.607 --> 00:03:13.276
 Load up, Neil, 
 let's get out of here, buddy. 

